        <ul class="tidy misconceptions">
          <li><b>"It works on my phone" is enough testing.</b> One device is one data point. Test a range: a small phone, a large phone, a tablet, and a real desktop window resize.</li>
          <li><b>Responsive design is finished once it "looks right."</b> Also check tap target sizes, zoom behavior, and load performance on throttled/mobile connections.</li>
          <li><b>Serving the largest image everywhere is "safer."</b> It's slower and wastes mobile data for no visual benefit — use <code>srcset</code>/<code>sizes</code> or <code>&lt;picture&gt;</code> instead.</li>
        </ul>

        <span class="callout-label" style="margin-top:18px;display:block;">Key takeaways</span>
